ctioning as de facto embassies. Taiwan is represented by the Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the United States, while the U.S. government is represented by the American Institute in Taiwan.","extract_html":"<p><b>Taiwan–United States relations</b> are unofficial and informal. Both sides maintain representative offices functioning as <i>de facto</i> embassies. Taiwan is represented by the Taipei Economic and Cultural Representative Office in the United States, while the U.S. government is represented by the American Institute in Taiwan.</p>"}